 "drivingQuestion": "Which earth is used to produce the 'earth water' standard?",
 "outcome": "not_dialectical",
 "outcomeNote": "Tannaitic positions recorded without decision.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "niddah.20a.22",
   "daf": "20a",
   "sentenceId": 21,
   "he": "וּכְמֵימֵי אֲדָמָה. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: כְּמֵימֵי אֲדָמָה — מֵבִיא אֲדָמָה שְׁמֵנָה מִבִּקְעַת בֵּית כֶּרֶם, וּמֵצִיף עָלֶיהָ מַיִם, דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי מֵאִיר. רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא אוֹמֵר: מִבִּקְעַת יוֹדְפַת. רַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: מִבִּקְעַת סִכְנִי. רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן אוֹמֵר: אַף מִבִּקְעַת גִּנּוֹסַר וְכַיּוֹצֵא בָּהֶן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «And» what is the color that is «like water» that inundates red «earth» that is impure? In this regard «the Sages taught» in a baraita: In order to examine blood that is «like water» that inundates red «earth, one brings fertile earth from the Beit Kerem Valley and one inundates» the earth with enough «water» until it pools on the surface; this is «the statement of Rabbi Meir. Rabbi Akiva says:» One brings earth «from the Yodfat Valley. Rabbi Yosei says: From the Sikhnei Valley. Rabbi Shimon says:» One can «even» bring earth «from the Genosar Valley or» from «similar» places."
  }
 ],
